The changes Guile needs to run under WebAssembly, in three groups.

Indirect-call signatures: wasm verifies the type of every call through a function pointer,
where a native target just jumps. Guile casts void(void) subr initializers and two-argument
hash callbacks into other pointer types, and each of those traps here. Each one is given a
wrapper with the signature the call site declares.

Word size: the compiler bakes in the host's pointer size when it cross-compiles Scheme to
bytecode, so a build machine with 64-bit pointers emits code that a 32-bit wasm target cannot
load. Read the target word size at run time instead.

Threads and locales: no pthreads and no locale support in this build, so the pieces that assume
either are compiled out.
